.\" Written by hand from lib/common.sh (require_config, build_exclude_params)
.\" and libexec/archivectl/*.sh; keep it in step with them.
.TH ARCHIVECTL.BORGBACKUP 5 2026-11-15 "archivectl" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
archivectl.borgbackup, .borgbackup \- backup source configuration for archivectl
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I <directory>/.borgbackup
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B archivectl init
writes
.I .borgbackup
into the directory it is to back up.
Every other command of
.BR archivectl (1)
finds the nearest one in the current directory or its parents, changes
into the directory that holds it, and reads it with the shell's
.B source
builtin: the file is a bash script, run with the user's rights, and may
set any variable.
.PP
These variables are read:
.TP
.B BORG_REPO
The Borg repository, a local path or an
.B ssh://
or scp-style URL.
Required by every command but
.BR init ,
which sets it to
.I $BORG_BACKUP_ROOT/<name>
or the location
.B \-\-repo
gives.
.TP
.B BORG_PASSCOMMAND
The command that prints the passphrase,
.B pass show archivectl/<name>
as
.B init
writes it when it keeps the passphrase in
.BR pass (1);
every command exports it for its borg calls.
.TP
.B BORG_RSH
The command borg reaches another host with, exported for borg when set;
.B init
writes the one set in its environment for a repository on another host.
.TP
.B SOURCE_DIR
What
.B create
archives,
.B diff
compares and
.B restore
extracts into, relative to the directory of the file.
Required by those three;
.B init
sets it to
.BR ./ .
.TP
.B EXCLUDES
A bash array of patterns
.B create
passes to
.B borg create
as
.BI \-\-exclude " pattern"
each, and
.B diff
to
.B rsync
as
.BI \-\-exclude= pattern
when it compares the live source.
When it is not set the patterns are
.BR .cache ,
.B tmp
and
.BR __pycache__ .
.PP
When no directory at or above the current one holds the file, the
command ends with status 1; a file that leaves a required variable empty
ends it with status 3.
.B init
writes every value quoted for the shell
.RB ( "printf %q" ),
so that a
.BR $ ,
a backquote or a space in a path stays part of it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
# Backup repository configuration for /home/user/papers
SOURCE_DIR=./
BORG_REPO=/data/backup/borg/home__user__papers
BORG_PASSCOMMAND=pass\e show\e \e'archivectl/home__user__papers\e'
EXCLUDES=(".cache" "node_modules" "*.log")
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR archivectl (1),
.BR borg (1),
.BR pass (1)
